11
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:36,000
An American Haunting is a 2005 historical supernatural horror film written and directed by Courtney
Solomon and starring Donald Sutherland, Sissy Spacek, James D'Arcy, and Rachel Hurd-Wood.

12
00:45:16,363 --> 00:45:22,363
It is based on the novel The Bell Witch: An American
Haunting (1995) by Brent Monahan.

13
00:49:02,727 --> 00:49:08,727
The events in the novel are loosely based on the legend of the Bell Witch, who
allegedly haunted the Bell family in rural 1810s Tennessee.

14
00:52:49,090 --> 00:52:55,090
The film documents the Bell family's supernatural experiences, which are paralleled with a contemporary
21st-century subplot involving a young girl plagued by similar events experienced by Betsy Bell.

15
00:56:35,454 --> 00:56:41,454
An international co-production between the United Kingdom, Canada, Romania, and the United
States, An American Haunting was filmed on location in Romania in the fall of 2004.

16
01:00:21,818 --> 01:00:27,818
An American Haunting was first previewed at the AFI Film Festival on November 5, 2005; it screened the same day at the San Sebastián
International Film Festival's "Fantasy and Horror Film Week." The film was released in the United Kingdom on April 14, 2006.

17
01:04:08,181 --> 01:04:14,181
Freestyle Releasing distributed the film theatrically in the United States on May
5, 2006 in an alternate cut from the version previously released.

18
01:07:54,545 --> 01:08:00,545
It received largely unfavorable reviews from film critics, though some
did praise it for its performances and period details.

19
01:11:40,909 --> 01:11:46,909
The film grossed $29.6 million worldwide against a $14 million budget.

20
01:15:27,272 --> 01:15:33,272
The film explores themes of witch, suitor, curse, family.

21
01:19:13,636 --> 01:19:19,636
The tone is mind_bending and dark and intense.
